<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1828" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ălĭca</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		from alo, acc. to Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
			7</span></i> Müll.; akin to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέω,
				ὀλαί</span> acc. to Doed., orig. adj.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>nourishing</i>,
			sc. farina. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of grain</i>, <i>spelt</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 76 <i>init.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 18, 7, 10, §
			50</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Grits prepared from it</i>, <i>spelt-grits</i>, Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόνδρος</span>,
			later <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλιξ</span>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 6,
			6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22, 25, 61, §
			128</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A drink prepared from these grits</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 13,
			6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>